WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.004
Rachel Okafor: Hi both, thanks for making time. How's the week going in Columbus?

2
00:00:09.265 --> 00:00:17.257
Patricia Hale: Busy. We're in the middle of open enrollment for the small group book, but the contact center side has been steady.

3
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:27.795
Luis Ortega: Steady is one word for it. We're right around 11,400 calls a week across claims and policy service, up maybe 4% over last month.

4
00:00:29.073 --> 00:00:37.076
Rachel Okafor: That tracks with what I saw in the dashboard. Is the after-hours claims pilot still where you want it, or are you tweaking hours?

5
00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:48.243
Luis Ortega: Still 6pm to 8am and weekends. The Voice Agent is picking up about 62% of those without a transfer now, which is better than I expected three weeks in.

6
00:00:48.941 --> 00:00:57.066
Patricia Hale: And the transcripts are landing in Genesys and Salesforce the way we hoped, so the adjusters aren't chasing notes.

7
00:00:57.804 --> 00:01:02.187
Rachel Okafor: Good. Any staffing changes I should note for the QM scorecards?

8
00:01:02.914 --> 00:01:11.440
Luis Ortega: We've got two new team leads starting Monday, so I'll need their QM seats turned on. I'll send their names over after this.

9
00:01:12.076 --> 00:01:16.720
Rachel Okafor: Perfect. And Patricia, how's the distribution side looking heading into Q4?

10
00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:25.185
Patricia Hale: Fine. The Google Ads offline conversions are still matching well, and Adobe is showing the campaign attribution we need. Nothing urgent there.

11
00:01:25.459 --> 00:01:32.767
Rachel Okafor: Okay. Anything from the pilot team you want me to capture while we're all on the line?

12
00:01:33.506 --> 00:01:42.747
Luis Ortega: Actually, yeah. One thing keeps coming up from our compliance folks, and it's worth putting in front of your product team.

13
00:01:44.128 --> 00:01:44.928
Rachel Okafor: Go ahead.

14
00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:55.049
Luis Ortega: On the claims side, our transcripts and the AI summaries can still carry things like policy numbers, dates of birth, and driver's license numbers.

15
00:01:55.049 --> 00:02:08.373
Luis Ortega: Our compliance group wants redaction we can configure ourselves, not a fixed setting, so we can decide what gets masked in transcripts and summaries and who on our side is allowed to see the unmasked version.

16
00:02:09.331 --> 00:02:14.031
Rachel Okafor: So configurable redaction of identifiers, with role-based access tied to it?

17
00:02:14.312 --> 00:02:27.746
Luis Ortega: Right, and audit so we can show who viewed what. The other piece is retention. We'd want transcripts to auto-delete after a set period we choose, say 90 days for the after-hours claims calls, and have that run on its own.

18
00:02:28.126 --> 00:02:39.020
Patricia Hale: That last part matters for our state filings. If we can set the window ourselves and prove it's enforced, that's a much easier conversation with the auditors.

19
00:02:40.241 --> 00:02:46.278
Rachel Okafor: Got it. Is this specific to the Voice Agent calls, or does it apply to live-agent calls too?

20
00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:55.109
Luis Ortega: Both, honestly. The after-hours pilot is where it surfaced, but the same rules should hold for anything a licensed agent handles.

21
00:02:56.411 --> 00:03:00.718
Rachel Okafor: How urgent is it? I want to set the right expectation internally.

22
00:03:02.131 --> 00:03:11.483
Luis Ortega: Medium. Nothing is on fire, but our next internal audit window is early next year, so it would be good to have an answer before then.

23
00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:22.833
Rachel Okafor: That's helpful. I'll write it up with the examples you gave and take it to the product team. I can't promise a date, but I'll come back with what I hear.

24
00:03:23.044 --> 00:03:24.597
Luis Ortega: That's all I'm asking.

25
00:03:25.203 --> 00:03:31.520
Patricia Hale: One more scheduling thing. Can we move the November review? The second week is heavy for us.

26
00:03:32.471 --> 00:03:42.548
Rachel Okafor: Sure. I'll send a couple of options for the week after. And I'll get the two QM seats provisioned once I have the names.

27
00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:45.147
Luis Ortega: I'll send them today.

28
00:03:45.832 --> 00:03:50.306
Rachel Okafor: Anything else on the pilot you want me to look at before then?

29
00:03:51.607 --> 00:03:55.380
Luis Ortega: No, the rest is running fine. Call volumes, routing, all good.

30
00:03:56.835 --> 00:04:02.651
Rachel Okafor: Great. I'll follow up with the write-up and the scheduling options by Monday. Thanks, both.

31
00:04:03.485 --> 00:04:04.314
Patricia Hale: Thanks, Rachel.

32
00:04:05.088 --> 00:04:06.434
Luis Ortega: Appreciate it. Talk soon.
